#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186238854 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186238937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239462 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186238937 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240761 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f5a8c5d5-fcb2-5bdd-8555-14fa5c61c1d7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240996 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240600 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240996 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105173" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240996 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240996 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of real polynomials of degree at most $1,$ and let the inner product on $V$ be defined as\n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1).\n$$\n\nNow consider the following elements of $V:$\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=5t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=-2t+2,\\,q(t)=-t-4\n$$\n\nFind the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $S=\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ given that ${p}_{1}(t)⊥{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the inner product, and that the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{1}(t)\\}$ equals $-5t.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240996 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38abb364-8716-52b0-b273-cfd769e1ebaf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240996 #edb/ref 1074 "Since the set $\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t)\\}$ is orthogonal, the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto the subspace $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t)={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t).\n$$\n\nWe are given that ${\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)=-5t,$ so let's now find the orthogonal projection of $q(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{{p}_{2}(t)\\}.$ This can be computed as\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t)=\\frac{⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}{⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩}\\,{p}_{2}(t).\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨q(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & =q(0){p}_{2}(0)+q(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(-t-4){|}_{0}\\cdot (-2t+2){|}_{0}+(-t-4){|}_{1}\\cdot (-2t+2){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot 2+(-5)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-8,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{2}(t)⟩ & ={p}_{2}(0){p}_{2}(0)+{p}_{2}(1){p}_{2}(1) \\\\  & =(-2t+2)^{2}{|}_{0}+(-2t+2)^{2}{|}_{1} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}+{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) & =\\frac{-8}{4}\\cdot (-2t+2)=4t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,q(t) & ={\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{1}(t)}\\,q(t)+{\\text{proj}}_{{p}_{2}(t)}\\,q(t) \\\\  & =-5t+(4t-4) \\\\  & =-t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241063 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240734 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241063 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105475" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241063 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241063 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V=C[0,1],$ the vector space of functions that are continuous over $[0,1].$ Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t,\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=4t-2$ with respect to the inner product." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241063 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5d460b9a-6ed3-5d23-955f-f3e1840b55a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241063 #edb/ref 1074 "The orthogonal projection of $f(t)$ onto $\\text{Span}\\{g(t)\\}$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t) & =\\frac{⟨f(t),g(t)⟩}{⟨g(t),g(t)⟩}\\,g(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}8t\\cdot (4t-2)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(4t-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(32{t}^{2}-16t)\\,\\text{d}t}{{\\int }_{0}^{1}(16{t}^{2}-16t+4)\\,\\text{d}t}\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{[\\frac{32}{3}{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}]_{0}^{1}}{[\\frac{16}{3}{t}^{3}-8{t}^{2}+4t]_{0}^{1}}\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{32}{3}-8)-0}{(\\frac{16}{3}-4)-0}\\cdot (6t-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{3})}{(\\frac{4}{3})}\\cdot (4t+2) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (4t-2) \\\\  & =8t-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe distance between $f(t)=8t$ and the subspace spanned by $g(t)=4t-2$ with respect to our inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-{\\text{proj}}_{g(t)}\\,f(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-(8t-4)‖ \\\\  & =‖4‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨4,4⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨4,4⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}4\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}16\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =16t\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =16-0 \\\\  & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{16}=4.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241070 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186240508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241070 #edb/ref 1069 "q-105496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241070 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241070 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $V={R}_{1}[t],$ the vector space of polynomials of degree at most $1$ with real coefficients. Given that the inner product on $V$ is defined as \n\n$$\n⟨p(t),q(t)⟩=p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nfind the distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the inner product." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241070 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0a9984c7-9d50-53ab-9302-5dd592a189c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186241070 #edb/ref 1074 "The distance between $f(t)=8t-3$ and $g(t)=3t+2$ with respect to the given inner product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =‖f(t)-g(t)‖ \\\\  & =‖8t-3-(3t+2)‖ \\\\  & =‖5t-5‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨5t-5,5t-5⟩ & =(5t-5){|}_{0}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{0}+(5t-5){|}_{1}\\cdot (5t-5){|}_{1} \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot (-5)+0\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the distance is $d=\\sqrt{25}=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186413797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1045 "Projecting Vectors Onto Subspaces in Inner Product Spaces" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186413797 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046660 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050841 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413792 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "fba5b1da-9880-515c-af94-05681b35cd3b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413793 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413793 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0a412cdd-29f8-5273-ab55-2a8dce391dae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413793 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134064 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413794 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413793 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413794 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "0bc7e18b-fdb5-5429-828f-e671a9abcbda" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413794 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241003 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413795 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186413796 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413795 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b37fdbb-b243-534e-930c-c4161c64569a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413795 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241059 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413796 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5b4d4a19-f8e8-5a9a-8c13-582c4e2b0863" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186413796 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186241063 #edb/ref 175921860454